    "created_at": "2017-05-30T09:49:04Z",
    "updated_at": "2017-05-30T09:49:04Z",
    "body": "> It would be tempting to just add \"hr { display:flow-root; }\" to the UA stylesheet.\r\n\r\nThere's some risk that it would break pages that specify `display: block` on `hr` and still expect it to avoid floats, though. Adding `!important` is possible but doesn't match what browsers do now, since they allow changing it to e.g. `display: inline`. I haven't analyzed web compat for this though.",
