    "updated_at": "2017-05-30T12:32:31Z",
    "body": "I went through the list of sites potentially affected by this, and I found:\r\n\r\nhttp://www.digitalremedy.com/\r\nhttp://www.prepary.com/\r\nhttp://www.acphs.edu/\r\n\r\nThey all use some tricks to get small knobs on each side of a HR.\r\n\r\nThe remaining sites were false alarms, either because the HR itself already established a BFC (by floating it or using overflow:hidden), or because there were no hr:before/after selectors at all (but rather class name selectors that ended with \"hr\").\r\n\r\nhttp://www.prepary.com/ actually looks the same to me with Blink's current rendering and if I turn it into a proper BFC. Same with http://www.acphs.edu/ . http://www.digitalremedy.com/ we have already discussed, and I'm pretty sure that the new rendering is unintentional (the top and bottom borders are no longer adjacent). But that's how Edge already renders it.\r\n\r\nGecko seems to steer clear of preceding floats and at the same time let floats inside a HR take part in one and the same BFC as the rest. Looks good, but this AvoidsFloats() behavior isn't covered in any spec, is it?  Blink is buggy: http://software.hixie.ch/utilities/js/live-dom-viewer/?saved=5214",
    "author_association": "NONE",
