    "created_at": "2017-05-30T13:39:25Z",
    "updated_at": "2017-05-30T13:43:38Z",
    "body": "So I guess EdgeHTML implements this by having `hr { overflow: hidden }` as UA style rule (and this is also [reflected with `getComputedStyle`](http://software.hixie.ch/utilities/js/live-dom-viewer/saved/5216)). That approach seems attractive for several reasons:\r\n\r\n* It is Web-compatible enough that Edge could ship with this behavior.\r\n* It avoids having custom code for `hr`.\r\n* Compared to `hr { display: flow-root }` as UA style, it is still a BFC even if the author specifies `hr { display: block }`.\r\n* It allows Web developers to opt out of `hr` being a BFC by changing 'overflow'.\r\n\r\nOf the affected sites, it's not really clear to me if they intended the Edge rendering or not. (Edit: I suppose http://www.acphs.edu/ intended the knobs to be there, and they're missing in Edge.) But at least they are not unacceptably broken either way.\r\n\r\nI don't think AvoidFloats() sans BFC is specified anywhere, and it would be nice to get rid of it.",
